---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Disclaimer | ShouldISpend"
  description="Read the Should I Spend disclaimer about calculator estimates, financial education, professional advice, and decision limits."
>
  <main class="trust-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Disclaimer</p>

    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>

    <p class="updated">Last reviewed: July 2026</p>

    <p class="intro">
      ShouldISpend provides educational calculators, spending-pressure scores,
      guides, examples, and general financial explanations. The site is designed
      to help users think through spending decisions more clearly, but it does
      not provide personalized professional advice.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Not Financial, Legal, Tax, Insurance, Medical, or Investment Advice</h2>

      <p>
        The information on ShouldISpend is for general educational and
        informational purposes only. It should not be treated as financial,
        legal, tax, insurance, medical, investment, lending, credit, or debt
        settlement advice.
      </p>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend is not a financial planning firm, lender, credit counselor,
        insurance agency, investment adviser, law firm, tax preparer, medical
        provider, or debt-relief company. No page on this site creates a
        professional-client relationship.
      </p>

      <p>
        Users should consult qualified professionals when a decision involves
        large debts, legal obligations, taxes, insurance claims, medical bills,
        bankruptcy risk, long-term contracts, or other complex personal
        circumstances.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How to Use Calculator Results</h2>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend calculators use simplified assumptions and the information
        entered by the user. A result may describe a decision as comfortable,
        manageable, aggressive, or risky, but that verdict is only a general
        estimate based on the inputs provided.
      </p>

      <p>
        A low-pressure result does not mean a purchase is automatically wise.
        A high-pressure result does not mean a purchase is impossible or never
        necessary. The calculators are intended to highlight tradeoffs, not make
        final decisions for users.
      </p>

      <p>
        Users are responsible for checking the numbers they enter and deciding
        whether the result fits their full situation. Local costs, taxes,
        family obligations, job stability, credit terms, insurance coverage,
        health needs, and emergency risks may all affect the real-world outcome.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Accuracy and Updates</h2>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend aims to provide useful, practical, and clear information.
        However, calculator formulas, examples, assumptions, and explanations
        may be incomplete, outdated, simplified, or different from a user's
        exact circumstances.
      </p>

      <p>
        The site may update pages, calculators, links, examples, or assumptions
        over time. ShouldISpend does not guarantee that every calculator result,
        guide, estimate, or recommendation-style explanation will apply to every
        person or remain current forever.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No Guarantees</h2>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend does not guarantee financial outcomes. Using a calculator
        or reading a guide cannot guarantee that a user will avoid debt, qualify
        for financing, receive assistance, save money, reduce expenses, or make
        the best possible decision.
      </p>

      <p>
        Financial decisions involve risk. Users should consider their full
        financial picture and use ShouldISpend as one educational input among
        other sources of information and judgment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Third-Party Links and Services</h2>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend may link to third-party websites, tools, services, data
        sources, or resources. Those links are provided for convenience and
        context. ShouldISpend does not control third-party sites and is not
        responsible for their content, policies, accuracy, pricing, or actions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Related Trust Pages</h2>

      <p>
        For more context, read the <a href="/about/">About</a> page,
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>, and
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. Questions or corrections
        can be sent through the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .trust-page {
      max-width: 880px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 72px 24px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      color: #0f766e;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4.4rem);
      line-height: 1;
      margin: 0 0 24px;
      color: #061126;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-top: 44px;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
      color: #061126;
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    p {
      color: #475569;
      line-height: 1.8;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    .intro {
      font-size: 1.16rem;
      color: #334155;
    }

    a {
      color: #0f766e;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .trust-closeout-section {
      margin-top: 32px;
      padding-top: 28px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .trust-closeout-section h2 {
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .trust-closeout-section p {
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
      margin: 0 0 16px;
    }

  </style>

      <section id="TrustDisclaimerCloseout" class="trust-closeout-section">
        <h2>Calculator results are estimates</h2>
        <p>
          Should I Spend provides calculators and educational content for planning
          purposes. Results depend on the numbers entered, the assumptions shown on the
          page, and the cost categories the reader includes. A result should not be
          treated as a guarantee, quote, approval, diagnosis, legal conclusion, or
          instruction to spend money.
        </p>
        <p>
          Actual costs may differ because of local prices, contract terms, fees,
          deposits, taxes, insurance, interest, medical needs, school policies, landlord
          requirements, lender rules, employer benefits, provider billing, travel dates,
          and other facts the site cannot verify for each reader.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="trust-closeout-section">
        <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
        <p>
          The site does not provide individualized financial, legal, tax, medical,
          insurance, real-estate, lending, or benefits advice. Readers should consult a
          qualified professional or the relevant provider when a decision has legal,
          medical, tax, credit, insurance, housing, or long-term financial consequences.
        </p>
        <p>
          Readers are responsible for checking actual quotes, contracts, bills,
          insurance requirements, loan terms, lease terms, provider policies, and due
          dates before making a commitment.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="trust-closeout-section">
        <h2>Use caution with close-call results</h2>
        <p>
          A close-call result should be treated as a reason to pause, not as permission
          to spend. If the decision only works when every assumption goes right, the
          safer next step may be to reduce the cost, wait, compare alternatives, build
          more savings, or ask a qualified professional for help.
        </p>
      </section>


      <section id="TrustDisclaimerCloseoutVerification" class="trust-closeout-section">
        <h2>Verify before committing money</h2>
        <p>
          Before acting on any result, readers should confirm the current price, fee,
          rate, bill, deposit, policy, contract term, appointment cost, cancellation
          rule, and due date with the organization involved. A calculator can organize a
          decision, but the final quote or agreement controls the real obligation.
        </p>
      </section>


      <section id="TrustDisclaimerCloseoutReaderResponsibility" class="trust-closeout-section">
        <h2>Reader responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          Readers are responsible for deciding whether a purchase, bill, lease, trip,
          payment plan, school expense, medical expense, funeral expense, or other
          spending decision fits their situation. The site can help organize the
          decision, but it cannot confirm private income, account balances, family
          obligations, credit terms, health needs, legal duties, or local requirements.
        </p>
        <p>
          When a result feels close, readers should pause and check whether the estimate
          still works after one normal problem: a higher quote, a delayed paycheck, an
          extra fee, a missed discount, a larger utility bill, or an unexpected repair.
        </p>
      </section>

      </Layout>
